# src/tychoc.c:8341 -- a bare None in a value-if branch is fixed only by a
# destination type, and neither `:=` nor `x : T =` flows one in.
# No pinned expectation: scored against ./tychoc1, which leaves an unfixed bare
# None at `?` and refuses this on the unused-local rule instead. Pinning either
# message would assert one compiler's wording as if it were both.
fn main():
    x := if true:
        None
    else:
        None
    println("hi")
